{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_ae459aa4c2d862dd3c7a06d916033f5c44b1da53748823231f638379a3969d3a", "title": "Sister Cupid", "text": "Sister Cupid is a 1987 Hong Kong romantic fantasy comedy film produced by and directed by Guy Lai and starring Jacky Cheung, Carol Cheng, Maggie Cheung and Pat Ha.", "score": 22.9852}, {"id": "hp_doc_c6711b6b2b7438491cad0b0fd90a4a37035b34a16342236f9f9ae0f85b258b0f", "title": "Maggie Cheung", "text": "Maggie Cheung Man-yuk (; born 20 September 1964) is a Hong Kong actress. Raised in Britain and Hong Kong, she has over 80 films to her credit since starting her career in 1983. Some of her most commercially successful works were in the action genre, but Cheung once said in an interview that of all the work she has done, the films that really meant something to her are \"Song of Exile\", \"Centre Stage\", \"\" and \"In the Mood for Love\". As Emily Wang in \"Clean\", her last starring role to date, she became the first Asian actress to win a prize at the Cannes Film Festival.", "score": 20.5756}, {"id": "hp_doc_2f409ccff7248c7e8841be18f6677ca80fe7b157430dc12fe63486d0451f1fda", "title": "Julian Cheung", "text": "Julian Cheung Chi-lam (born 27 August 1971), better known by his stage name Chilam, is a Hong Kong singer and actor. Cheung is popularly known for his role as Guo Jing in the 1994 TV series adaptation of the \"Wuxia\" novel, \"The Legend of the Condor Heroes\", and also as Chi-Kin from the TVB drama \"Cold Blood Warm Heart\" (1996).", "score": 11.6282}], "remaining_searches": 1}
